==================================================================
DAY 12 - PART B: LAB
Break a rollout, then roll back
Time: 75-90 minutes
==================================================================

cd ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week2


STEP 1: Start clean with change-cause annotations
-------------------------------------------------
k apply -f deploy-web.yaml          # from Day 11 (nginx:1.27 if you updated it)
k annotate deploy/web kubernetes.io/change-cause="initial deploy" --overwrite
k rollout history deploy/web


STEP 2: Build up some history
-----------------------------
k set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:1.26
k annotate deploy/web kubernetes.io/change-cause="downgrade to 1.26" --overwrite
k rollout status deploy/web

k set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:1.27-alpine
k annotate deploy/web kubernetes.io/change-cause="switch to alpine" --overwrite
k rollout status deploy/web

k rollout history deploy/web
k get rs -l app=web

You should see 3 revisions and 3 ReplicaSets (two at 0 replicas).


STEP 3: Inspect a revision
--------------------------
k rollout history deploy/web --revision=2
k get rs -l app=web -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,REV:.metadata.annotations.deployment\\.kubernetes\\.io/revision,IMAGE:.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image,READY:.status.readyReplicas


STEP 4: Deploy a broken version
-------------------------------
Terminal 2: k get pods -l app=web -w

k set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:9.9.9-doesnotexist
k annotate deploy/web kubernetes.io/change-cause="bad tag" --overwrite
k rollout status deploy/web --timeout=60s
echo "exit code: $?"         # non-zero = failed

k get pods -l app=web

Observe: ONE new pod is in ImagePullBackOff, the 3 old pods are still
Running (maxUnavailable: 0 protects you). Users would not notice.

k describe deploy web | grep -A5 Conditions


STEP 5: Roll back
-----------------
k rollout undo deploy/web
k rollout status deploy/web
k get pods -l app=web
k rollout history deploy/web

Notice: the revision you rolled back to got a new number, and the
bad revision is still listed.


STEP 6: Roll back to a specific revision
----------------------------------------
k rollout history deploy/web
Pick the "downgrade to 1.26" revision number (N):
  k rollout undo deploy/web --to-revision=N
  k get deploy web -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'


STEP 7: Progress deadline
-------------------------
k patch deploy web -p '{"spec":{"progressDeadlineSeconds":30}}'
k set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:broken-again
sleep 40
k get deploy web -o jsonpath='{range .status.conditions[*]}{.type}={.status} {.reason}{"\n"}{end}'

Expect: Progressing=False ProgressDeadlineExceeded
k rollout undo deploy/web


STEP 8: Limit the history
-------------------------
k patch deploy web -p '{"spec":{"revisionHistoryLimit":2}}'
k set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:1.27
k rollout status deploy/web
k get rs -l app=web           # only 2 old ReplicaSets kept
k rollout history deploy/web


STEP 9: Write a safe-deploy script
----------------------------------
vi ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week2/safe-deploy.sh

#!/bin/bash
# usage: ./safe-deploy.sh nginx:1.26
set -u
IMAGE=$1
kubectl set image deploy/web nginx=$IMAGE
kubectl annotate deploy/web kubernetes.io/change-cause="deploy $IMAGE" --overwrite
if ! kubectl rollout status deploy/web --timeout=60s; then
  echo "Rollout failed, rolling back"
  kubectl rollout undo deploy/web
  kubectl rollout status deploy/web
  exit 1
fi
echo "Deployed $IMAGE"

chmod +x safe-deploy.sh
./safe-deploy.sh nginx:1.26
./safe-deploy.sh nginx:nope


STEP 10: Clean up and commit
----------------------------
k delete deploy web
cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day12: rollbacks"
